<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Henry</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Henry is an American folk hero, a Black freedman said to have been a &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a>-driving man&quot;: with a hammer he drove a steel drill into rock to make holes for the explosives that blasted out railroad tunnels. According to the legend, his strength was measured in a race against a steam-powered rock drill. He won the race, but died in victory with the hammer in his hand, his heart giving out from the strain.</p></div>
